Host visuals as native views on Windows: GPUI's DirectComposition device for content that wants a visual of its own.

What: `gpui_windows::composition_device(window)` returns the DirectComposition device of GPUI's window (from its
window handle; `None` without DirectComposition or while the window draws), in a new file
`directx_renderer/native_view_host.rs`. `NativeView::new` on Windows now also takes an `IDCompositionVisual` made on
that device: `NativeViewTree::attach` adds it under the view's content visual (offset and clipped like any view)
instead of setting it as content; detaching removes it. After a lost device the views are attached again one by
one, a visual from the old device logged and skipped (it cannot join the new tree; the app makes it again) rather
than failing the whole recovery. Hooks: one module line, one `pub use`, doc lines on `attach_native_view` and
`NativeView::new`.

Why: owner decision 2026-11-27 (issue #1, WebView2). WebView2's visual hosting
(`CreateCoreWebView2CompositionController`) renders into a `RootVisualTarget`, a visual that must be on the device of
the tree it joins, so the app needs GPUI's device; with it, a WebView2 page is a NativeView like a swap chain, with
its input sent from the view element's listeners (`SendMouseInput`, `MoveFocus`; examples/native-view-webview2).

`gpui_windows::on_composition_device_changed(window, callback)` tells the app each time a lost GPU device gave the
window a new DirectComposition device, after its tree is rebuilt (`events.rs` calls it once the renderer's borrow
ends), since a visual made on the old device can't join the new tree: the app makes its visual (WebView2's
controller) and `NativeView` again. examples/native-view-webview2 does.

Test: `scripts/windows-native-view-checks.sh` runs examples/native-view-webview2 on CI's Windows runner at 100 and
125 %: the page renders in the hole under the cover div, a click, wheel and key over it reach the page (it posts
them back through `WebMessageReceived`), and GPUI draws 0 frames per second while only the page animates
(docs/native-view-windows.md).

Upstream PR: not filed (filing paused, patch rule 14).

